SWEET Bluetooth transport, kernel side (patch 0189, BT-S3 f; ticket T-7eba; docs/research/BT-S3-transport-decision.md D-1 = option (a), plain UART kctl). New bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c registers, when the ADT has the node /bluetooth (tools/mkadt.py, BT-S3 e): kctl "com.apple.uart.bluetooth" (BlueTool, matrix M17) and "com.apple.uart.sk.bluetooth" as the SAME plain control (M10', no Skywalk: M12-M14 not implemented), TIOCGETA/TIOCSETA sockopts (M15, M16), H4 send (M19), and the char devices /dev/btwake /dev/btpoweroff /dev/btreset (M11, M21-M23). A hook in the default case of ctl_ioctl (bsd/kern/kern_control.c) serves TIOCMGET (M20), which the stock kernel answered with a silent ENOTSUP. BT-S4a (T-e930) adds the backend bsd/dev/sweet_bt_uart.c (gs101 UART16 serial@175B0000 polled, USI mode, BT_REG_ON gpp16-2 / DEV_WAKE gpp14-3, power order A10/A27; enabled only by boot-arg sweetbt=1, store list in the file header) and the RX relay sweet_bt_rx; without sweetbt=1 there is NO backend, so every operation that needs one logs its "BT GAP:" line (matrix section 4 texts, first 8 calls and every power of two, " xN") and returns an error (ENOTSUP/ENXIO/EINVAL), never success; only a connect succeeds (control layer) and says so. A later patch supplies struct sweet_bt_ops via sweet_bt_set_ops(). The init is called from sweet_ufs_init and from the USB root disk init (idempotent). Termios mode, polarity of the switches and the node permissions (0666) are not measured: the polarity is BT-S3 O4 (open), the mode is a [guess]. Reads cannot be hooked (socket buffer), a missing RX path shows as M43. Not built on hardware, not run. Host test: tools/test_sweet_bt_c.py.
